<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg within-feather Turing wavelength of Anas platyrhynchos at 378.4 µm (Pass 1) (Anas platyrhynchos (Holocene, 0 Ma))",
        "Schnakenberg within-feather Turing wavelength of Anas platyrhynchos at 378.4 µm (Pass 1) faithfully reproduces Anas platyrhynchos (Holocene, 0 Ma) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Anas platyrhynchos (Holocene, 0 Ma) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Anas platyrhynchos (Holocene, 0 Ma)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That 378.4 µm was measured on a mallard feather in the cited papers.",
        "does_not_claim: That the green head or the speculum is a Turing pigment.",
        "does_not_claim: That the pass-1 vane GIF matches the drake photograph.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Near-onset deviation PDE with cubic saturation and an optional quadratic term q U^2.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: lambda_star pinned to the campaign anchor 0.0003784 m, not to a published mallard measurement.",
        "reported_in_source: Inaba & Chuong 2020: macro body pattern and micro within-feather pattern are different levels.",
        "reported_in_source: Prum & Williamson 2002: within-feather bars, stripes, and spots can be reaction-diffusion patterns.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v.",
        "reported_in_source: Stavenga et al. 2017: mallard speculum hue is a multilayer, not a pigment wavenumber.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the diffusion-driven instability conditions.",
        "transfer_boundary: The Anas chronoseries is 1/1 at 0 Ma. Scale neighbours (348 µm bioelectric, 1.3 mm vertex packing, 2.4 cm plumage block) are other laws or another length, not other chronospecies." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Anas platyrhynchos" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Aves (Ornithes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Anas" ;
